@reactions event.crossingLine.warning
// EW1 (events writer), Crossing the Line: from Saturday 08:00 (the user's line-q1 b; Vance's Mail stays at 18:00) to
// Sunday 14:30, crew talk about "the Line"; some ask "first crossing?". The lines say "tomorrow", so they read right all
// Saturday and the Sunday morning lines are the Sunday-only ones EV1 adds, if any.
? cue:event.crossingLine.warning
- We cross the Line tomorrow. First time? You'll love it. Mostly.   #funny
- First crossing? Lucky you. Don't drink the punch. You'll drink the punch.   #funny
- The Line's tomorrow. The horn goes on every deck. Don't jump.
- Tomorrow we cross into the Veyli reach. New stars out of the windows.
? cue:event.crossingLine.warning tier>=acquaintance
- First crossing, {nick}? Stand at the front tomorrow. That's the rule.
? cue:event.crossingLine.warning dept:galley
- Line punch tomorrow. Brennan's recipe. We don't ask what's in it.   #funny
? cue:event.crossingLine.warning dept:helm
- Tomorrow at half two we cross the Line. Helm's flying it. Gently.
? cue:event.crossingLine.warning dept:survey
- New reach, new charts. Survey's been waiting months for this.
? cue:event.crossingLine.warning tier>=friend
- I'll stand with you tomorrow. Everyone needs someone at their first Line.   #warm
? cue:event.crossingLine.warning who:pell
- My first Line was two years ago. I still dream about that punch.   #funny
// Holt's one line: the here and now only (his arc: nothing of borders, past crossings or the Veyli)
? cue:event.crossingLine.warning who:holt
- Crossing or no crossing, this ship stays tidy. No punch on my decks.

// EW2 (events writer 2), why the crossing matters (line plan, line-q10 A "guests in someone else's sky"; the user):
// old hands explain it in bits. The first two carry the Veyli fact (plans/veyli-lore-plan.md section 3). Never the
// visit, never why the Envoy is aboard, never Holt's border day or "last time"; "help is far" is distance, not danger.
? cue:event.crossingLine.warning !who:saruth|holt
- Past the Line every star's got a Veyli name. They got there first.
- Six hundred years the Veyli have been out there. We're the new ones.
- Past the Line we're guests in someone else's sky. Best manners, all of us.   #warm
- Help's a long way off out there. That's what the oath's about. Each other.
? cue:event.crossingLine.warning dept:survey !who:saruth
- Our charts go thin past the Line. A few runs, never a full survey. Until now.
